  "rule": "The Dipper Handle's own cut, and the handle's count (with the authored wish d9, When the Handle Loses Count). Each damaging Metal art you fire moves the handle one star, one star a breath at most: a second Metal art within 1 s of the last star moves none. Before the seventh star the handle loses count, and its stars are cleared, when you fire a damaging art that is not Metal (the basic attack, wards and heals never count); after a lost count it counts again once you have gone 3 s with no damaging or movement art. With seven stars or more this cut points east: it spends every star, strikes twice (two hits, twice the force in all) and each of its hits lays 1 Metal stack for 8 s; if one of those hits makes the foe Broken, the handle keeps 3 stars.",
