  "rule": "The Army-Breaker's waited thrust, and the spear's Momentum (with the authored wish d21, The Army Fights, the Marshal Waits). Each full second in which you fire no damaging or movement art adds 1 Momentum, and each second one of your companions' or summons' hits lands while you wait adds 1 more (their hits are not yours, so they keep your wait). Momentum loses a twentieth of itself each second; each second of waiting past the fifth costs 1 % of your linh lực. This thrust deals 5 % more for each Momentum, ignores the foe's block and passes half of its ward shields (bypass 0.5, the engine's cap), then spends all the Momentum. With full Momentum (10 or more) it also breaks the foe's guard open: Exposed for 3 s (the engine's reading of \"breaks one formation link or summoned ward\"). The basic attack does not break the wait (the Composed clock's rule).",
